The default local decision-router model, convaiinnovations/laya-typed-decisions
(https://huggingface.co/convaiinnovations/laya-typed-decisions), is licensed
Apache-2.0 and is not bundled with this repository; `scripts/setup-laya.ps1`
downloads it separately from Hugging Face at install time, pinned to a
validated revision. It is built on the ModernBERT-large encoder by Answer.AI
and LightOn. An alternative checkpoint, Luni/laya-grounded
(https://huggingface.co/Luni/laya-grounded), can be installed instead by
passing `-Repo` to `scripts/setup-laya.ps1`; it is licensed CC-BY-NC-4.0
(non-commercial), so anyone building a commercial product on top of POK-Ai
must not select it and should keep the Apache-2.0 default (see
`docs/decision-router-backends.md`).

The optional local cross-model judge, php-ai/zeiger-0.6b
(https://huggingface.co/php-ai/zeiger-0.6b), is licensed CC-BY-SA-4.0 (weights)
and is disabled by default. It is not bundled with this repository;
`scripts/setup-zeiger.ps1` downloads it separately from Hugging Face at
install time, pinned to a validated revision. CC-BY-SA-4.0 requires that
adaptations of the weights themselves (not POK-Ai's own source code, which
